  "test_harness_notes": [
    "The first NixOS test stopped at an obsolete assertion expecting inline MCP tools. OpenClaw 2026.10.1 exposes them through Tool Search. The updated fixture requires actual NixOS tool discovery and a Hypruse desktop call, and the case was repeated from a fresh disk."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Physical YubiKey sign-in/removal/unlock must be retested with the new greeter. Earlier owner-reported success belongs to earlier images.",
    "Real provider authentication, physical Wi-Fi, Secure Boot, encryption and non-US keyboard layouts were not qualified on these ISO bytes.",
    "The native custom fixture installs a minimal ext4 console system. The Quickshell login example is a separate source VM, not proof that every custom agent-generated configuration works.",
    "Boot-floor checks are structural and requirement evidence is agent-reported. Btrfs, XFS, custom encryption, alternative bootloaders and multi-disk workflows have no end-to-end qualification here.",
    "The custom native operations are scripted test fixtures, not unconstrained model-generated deployments. No independent byte-identical rebuild or physical Ventoy boot test was performed.",
    "The multi-key enrollment redesign and persistent installation status strip are not included."
  ]
